<article class="env-lemma" id="0FJD">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FJD">Lemma <span data-tag="0FJD">15.120.4</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  K \subset L \subset M  \]
</div>
  <p> be $R$-modules such that $K$, $L/K$, and $M/L$ are finite projective $R$-modules. Then the diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ \det (K) \otimes \det (L/K) \otimes \det (M/L) \ar[r] \ar[d] &  \det (L) \otimes \det (M/L) \ar[d] \\  \det (K) \otimes \det (M/K) \ar[r] &  \det (M) }  \]
</div>
  <p> commutes where the maps are those of Lemma <a href="/tag/0FJB" data-tag="0FJB">15.120.2</a>. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. Hint: after localizing at a prime of $R$ we can assume $K \subset L \subset M$ is isomorphic to $R^{\oplus a} \subset R^{\oplus a + b} \subset R^{\oplus a + b + c}$ and in this case the result is an evident computation. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>